[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2020.11.17"]
[UTCTime "19:10:37"]

{ Black has a bad Bishop, since he can not threaten White’s pawns. The white Knight can easily capture some of black's pawns. This would result in a promotion to a white Queen. However, there is a good move that Black can do. This move is to exchange his bad Bishop with the opponent’s valuable knight. With that exchange, Black will place himself in a better position and this can be decisive in winning the game. }
1... Bxg5 2. Kxg5 Ke3 3. Kf5 Kd3 4. Ke5 Kc3 5. Kd5 Kxb3 6. Kxc5 Kc3 7. Kb5 Kb3 8. Kc5 Kc3 9. Kb5 b3 { [%csl Gb2,Gb1,Gc5,Gc6,Gc7,Gc8] } *


