{ Create a defense by placing the bishop in such a way that together with the left front square of the pawn, the white king can only position himself behind the pawn so that he is always just one step too late. }
1. Bd7 { Ok that is smart. You position your Bishop to a place where it can defend the pawn removing only once } { [%csl Gg3,Gg4,Gd4,Gd3,Gd2,Gc8,Ge6,Gf5,Gh3,Gc6,Gb5,Ga4,Ge8] } 1... Ke3 (1... Kf3 2. Kd4 { [%csl Ge5,Ge4,Ge3,Gf5,Gg4,Gh3,Ge6,Ge8,Gc8,Gc6,Gb5,Ga4,Gg3] } 2... Kf4 { [%csl Gg4,Gf5,Ge6,Ge8,Gc8,Gc6,Gb5,Ga4,Gh3,Ge5,Ge4,Ge3,Gg3] } 3. h4 { [%csl Gg5,Gg4,Ge5,Ge4,Ge3,Gf5,Ge6,Ge8,Gc8,Gc6,Gb5,Ga4,Gh3] } 3... Kf3 { [%csl Gg5,Gf5,Gg4,Gh3,Ge6,Gc8,Ge8,Gc6,Gb5,Ga4,Ge5,Ge4,Ge3] } 4. h5 { [%csl Gg6,Gg4,Ge5,Ge4,Ge3] } 4... Kf4 5. h6 { [%csl Gg4,Gg7,Ge5,Ge4,Ge3] } 5... Kf3 $18 { No use chasing the pawn because you are a step too late. } 6. h7 Kf4 7. h8=Q $18) 2. h4 Ke4 3. h5 Ke5 4. h6 (4. Be8 Kf6 $18) 4... Kf6 5. Be8 $18 { Black can not proceed anyfurther to h8 to stop white from promotion of the pawn. } White wins


